## What Problem This Solves

Fixes unbounded memory growth in legacy `toolsBySender` deprecation warning deduplication. The `warnedLegacyToolsBySenderKeys` Set accumulated every warned legacy sender key forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap. A long-running gateway process parsing untyped `toolsBySender` keys retained entries for every distinct sender key that ever triggered a deprecation.

## Why This Change Was Made

Added a 4 096-entry LRU cap with touch-on-read on the private `warnedLegacyToolsBySenderKeys` Set. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow; frequently re-warned keys are promoted to MRU on access. The public `resolveToolsBySender` API is unchanged — only the private `warnLegacyToolsBySenderKey` helper routes through the new wrappers.

## User Impact

No change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct legacy `toolsBySender` keys — far beyond any realistic config. Gateways exceeding the cap may see one extra deprecation warning per evicted entry, a bounded trade-off versus the prior unbounded growth.

## Evidence

### Before fix: Set grows without bound

Feeding 5 000 distinct legacy keys through `resolveToolsBySender` (script: `live-proof-before.ts`):

```text
$ npx tsx live-proof-before.ts
Feeding 5000 distinct legacy keys through resolveToolsBySender...
→ 5000 deprecation warnings emitted (one per unique legacy key).
→ All 5000 entries permanently retained in the Set.
→ No eviction — this is the unbounded growth pattern the PR fixes.
```

### After fix: 4 096-entry LRU cap

Running the patched module through the same exercise (script: `live-proof.ts`):

```text
$ npx tsx live-proof.ts

=== Proof 2: With 4096-entry LRU cap, cache stays bounded ===
→ Seeded 4095 entries into the cache.
→ Resolved "legacy-key-0" — cache is now at 4096 entries (exactly at cap).
→ Pushed 5 extra entries past the cap.
→ Re-resolving "legacy-key-1" after eviction...
→ "legacy-key-1" was re-warned (evicted from cache).

=== Proof 3: LRU touch-on-read keeps hot keys from eviction ===
→ After 42 LRU touches, "legacy-key-2" survived (LRU touch working).

=== Summary ===
4096-entry LRU cap verified:
  1. Cache stays at 4096 entries maximum.
  2. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow.
  3. Frequently re-warned entries survive via LRU touch-on-read.
```

